{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 formalization of the ordered adjacency spectrum of finite prime-cover graphs. For every fixed finite set S of deleted primes and epsilon > 0, uniformly over allowed centres a <= (log X)^(1/2-epsilon), it proves that the square of the eigenvalue at the arithmetic rank j(a) equals pi_S(X/a) plus four times the finite allowed-prime sum of 1/(p-1), plus c(a) + o(1). This is the manuscript's elementary finite-sum form of its uniform constant-layer theorem.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Idris Ali Shaik"
    }
  ],
